You are Einstein's improvement executor for TESSERA Round 3 candidate R3-06.

## Goal
Improve `trimToBudget` in artifacts/api-server/src/lib/prompt-builder.ts so truncation keeps BOTH the head and the tail of a chunk (token-budget efficiency: key facts often sit at the end). Round-1 KEEP build 09 showed head/tail / coverage-preserving cuts keep more needle paragraphs than head-only.

## Current
```
function trimToBudget(text: string, maxTokens: number): string {
  const maxChars = maxTokens * APPROX_CHARS_PER_TOKEN;
  if (text.length <= maxChars) return text;
  return text.slice(0, maxChars - 30) + "\n…[truncated]";
}
```

## Change to
```
function trimToBudget(text: string, maxTokens: number): string {
  const maxChars = maxTokens * APPROX_CHARS_PER_TOKEN;
  if (text.length <= maxChars) return text;
  const marker = "\n…[truncated]\n";
  const budget = Math.max(16, maxChars - marker.length);
  const head = Math.ceil(budget * 0.6);
  const tail = budget - head;
  return text.slice(0, head) + marker + text.slice(text.length - tail);
}
```

Export `trimToBudget` for testing OR test via `buildPrompt` with a long retrieved chunk that has a unique needle only near the end.

## Add test
artifacts/api-server/src/__tests__/prompt-builder-trim.test.ts:
1. Build a long string: `"HEAD_MARK " + "x".repeat(5000) + " TAIL_NEEDLE_42"`
2. Under a tight budget where head-only would drop the needle, assert the new trim keeps both HEAD_MARK and TAIL_NEEDLE_42.
3. Measure needle retention: for 20 synthetic docs each with a unique needle planted in the last 10% of characters, under a budget of 30% of length, count how many needles survive head-only vs head+tail. Assert head+tail > head-only. Log `PROMPT_TRIM needles headOnly=A headTail=B n=20`.

You may implement head-only inline in the test solely as the baseline comparator (do not leave head-only in production).

Also run any existing prompt-builder related tests if present.

## Constraints
- Do NOT flip enable flags; no deletes; no history rewrite
- Only prompt-builder.ts + new test
- Branch: einstein/r3-06-prompt-head-tail-trim
- NON-DRAFT PR: "Einstein R3-06: head+tail trimToBudget keeps end needles"
- Await CI; do NOT merge
- Return PR URL, CI, needle retention before→after

